## Notes
- PSD white floor S = 22824.8 ± 12.3 cps (expected 22854.0); cross-PSD floor offset = -7.5 ± 4.9 cps (vanishes).
- Shift register with nominal Pu-239 moments (8.240, 17.321): m_Pu = 443.8 g (+47.9%), M = 1.140, alpha = 0.148 -> OpenMC implicit fission does not reproduce induced-fission multiplicity; effective moments required.
- 2B with the single-exponential (spec) kernel: D_inf = 17116, T_inf = 13191 (biased low, chain timing not exponential); m_Pu = 306.1 g (partial cancellation). The free two-component kernel removes the bias.
- Shift register / 2A T_inf use f_t from iid capture-time draws; correlated chain timing (thermal-return fission) makes this f_t ~3% too high -> T_inf ~3% low -> m_Pu ~+4%. The bispectrum needs no gate-fraction calibration.
- 2A reproduces the shift-register moments exactly (r1 = f1-b1, r2 = (f2-b2)-b1(f1-b1)): the deconvolution removes the accidental cross-term automatically.
